{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462886-anybody-ever-played-a-fomor","id":1462886,"title":"Anybody ever played a Fomor?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-06T05:49:08-07:00","id":1462886,"title":"Anybody ever played a Fomor?","content":"Has anybody her tired to play the Freak Legion supplement or the Guide to Possessed character? If yes, can you tell me your stories?<br /> <br /> <br /> Aaaand...<br /> can you come up with a Taint / Power build that would be able to go toe to toe with a crinos?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27051,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","user":"Solomon Draak","date":". 10-06-2021, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T15:45:47-07:00","id":1463032,"title":"","content":"We did try it once almost 20 years ago. It was silly and unnecessary edgy. We kinda gave up rather quickly as beyond the actual chargen and characters being weird and freaky and the powers provoking a lot of laughter, the actual activities, needs and deterioration of Fomori quickly came to the fore. For all its unnecessary splatter aesthetics the book drove forward quite well how broken and messed up fomori are and made us drop it.<br /> <br /> I got way more mileage out of the Book of the Wyrm/Wyld/Weaver and Possesed for actual games to use them as supporting cast, enemies and antagonists.<br /> <br /> As for building something that can go toe to toe with a Crinos, depends on the Crinos, and how much extra points you get to make the character. Mostly because you need high stats, ability to soak aggravated damage, armor and either claws or weapons made to kill Werewolves. Not very likely with the way the default spread looks like and how short a shelf life combat fomori have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 10-07-2021, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T00:51:07-07:00","id":1466913,"title":"","content":"I find that the book is excellent for crafting antagonistic NPCs, and there are some pretty unique ways it could happen. I seem to recall that there were some traits that involved having calloused skin that their claws could become lodged in, leaving them prone to attack, even if the fomor itself dies. As for specific fomor archetypes, the Hollow Men are fantastic and make the book alone worth owning. As for actually playing, basically same as above. Nobody was really into it and mostly just had fun with the idea. There was another, forgot the name, that could attack people from the toilet. Just, really great NPC material IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T15:05:47-08:00","id":1467201,"title":"","content":"I've twice been part of a game where we played the villagers from The Shadow Over Innsmouth, once as Rokea kinfolk, and the other as what were essentially Deep One spawn. Both eventually ended up with going against what became the FBI-SAD (or Delta Green if you prefer). It was interesting, but we all played it pretty straight, in what was a fairly grim and run down Depression era New England fishing town. <br /> <br /> The one shot of being various slasher-type killers at a horror convention vs Garou was less serious. Partially because we were able to keep re-spawning (usually by taking over another victim) after being killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T05:20:12-08:00","id":1467870,"title":"","content":"I think that fomori is a great character idea for one player game where his characters experience changes caused by the bane (maybe his parents didn't tell him that he was born in a Petrie dish, in Freak Legion there was even a firm that was creating fomori that way) and the rest of the characters are mortals (maybe one, but no more is a callow kinfolk, lost revenant or sth like that) trying to help him. It could be some kind of Stephen King small town story, during which you go first to the priest, than a local witch and in the end you could stomp on a sept and try to convince them to help you not by tearing you apart. The ending could be like that: if the characters were fast enough the bane is too weak to resist the Rite of Cleansing and the fomori is saved, if not it is killed. Then the garou try to wipe out the memories of PCs the easiest way they know: by shifting into crinos and let the Delirium do the work. The ending I would run as a description rather than the game. It could be something like that: one character never recovered from the experience. He ended his life by his own hand/institutionalised. The second one had nightmares every night since then. He tried professional help, autotherapy by writing rather succesful horror stories and died when he returned to the sept only to be slaughtered by its guardians. The third one decided that life is too unpredictable so he &quot;lived&quot; it on 10, by drinking, taking drugs and casual sex. This character could be an NPC for your regular campaign. The fourth one... etc. Yeah, I know, looks like &quot;Stand by me&quot;, again thank you Steven \ud83d\ude42. But basically, I think it should be an one-shot story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-15-2021, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T08:17:18-08:00","id":1467883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462886-anybody-ever-played-a-fomor?p=1463032#post1463032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for building something that can go toe to toe with a Crinos, depends on the Crinos, and how much extra points you get to make the character. Mostly because you need high stats, ability to soak aggravated damage, armor and either claws or weapons made to kill Werewolves. Not very likely with the way the default spread looks like and how short a shelf life combat fomori have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree. The only power you need is Delirium Immunity. The rest can be replaced with M-4 or a pair of MP5 with a few clips of silver ammo. Believe me, a team of such fomori could wipe out an entire sept (that's why I use this combination rarely, just like snipers or demolition experts; PCs almost always have no chance against them).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T17:05:32-08:00","id":1467944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1462886-anybody-ever-played-a-fomor?p=1467870#post1467870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ending I would run as a description rather than the game. It could be something like that: one character never recovered from the experience. He ended his life by his own hand/institutionalised. The second one had nightmares every night since then. He tried professional help, autotherapy by writing rather succesful horror stories and died when he returned to the sept only to be slaughtered by its guardians. The third one decided that life is too unpredictable so he &quot;lived&quot; it on 10, by drinking, taking drugs and casual sex. This character could be an NPC for your regular campaign. The fourth one... etc. Yeah, I know, looks like &quot;Stand by me&quot;, again thank you Steven \ud83d\ude42. But basically, I think it should be an one-shot story.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a similar story I would let each player build their character's aftermath. But this story may also serve as background for some of those characters in another game as supernaturals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}